-- title:
--   Surjectivity of a diamond endomorphism of the finite chart algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, containing a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$; let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $j \in K$ be a nonzero element whose Laurent expansion is the coefficient image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant. Let $d$ be coprime to $Mp$, and let $\theta$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ which, under the identification of elements by their Laurent expansions, agrees with the base change to $L$ of the diamond automorphism [`ModularCurve.diamondAut (M * p) d`](def/ModularCurve_X1Diamond.html#L66). Finally, let $\rho$ be a ring endomorphism of the subalgebra `chartAlgFin A K j` of elements of $K$ integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by $j$, whose values agree with $\theta$ in $K$. Then $\rho$ is surjective.
--
--   This records that the endomorphism induced by a diamond operator $\langle d \rangle$ on the $j$-finite chart algebra of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring above $p$ in $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ is onto, the point being that $\theta$ is an automorphism preserving $A[j]$ and hence its integral closure. It is used to show that such a diamond operator fixes each minimal prime over the uniformiser, i.e. preserves the components of the special fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_surjective_of_apply_eq_diamondAut_chartAlgFin_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul.lean

